# [FABLE-5] sq-hmd7l.10 — vendored ORE-style CLASS-SATISFIABILITY task
# (expected: ontology CONSISTENT, class :MadCow UNSATISFIABLE).
# Hand-authored, hand-verified — the classic "mad cow" pattern from DL tutorials/ORE
# satisfiability tasks: MadCow ⊑ Vegetarian ⊓ ∃eats.Meat while Vegetarian ⊑ ∀eats.¬Meat,
# so any MadCow instance needs an eats-successor that is both Meat and ¬Meat (clash on
# every branch). The ontology ITSELF stays consistent (MadCow may simply be empty:
# daisy ∈ Vegetarian has no eats-successor).
@prefix : <http://sparq.dev/bench/ore-smoke/madcow#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

:Vegetarian rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :eats ;
                              owl:allValuesFrom [ owl:complementOf :Meat ] ] .
:MadCow rdfs:subClassOf :Vegetarian .
:MadCow rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :eats ;
                          owl:someValuesFrom :Meat ] .

:daisy a :Vegetarian .
